homoeopathic-materia-medica-repertory-json — Licensing
======================================================

This repository holds two kinds of material under two different licences.  They
do not conflict: each folder is covered by exactly one of them, and the folder
that is GPL v3 is listed explicitly below.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
1.  Compiled public-domain datasets  —  CC0 1.0 Universal
--------------------------------------------------------------------
The person who associated these works with this deed has dedicated them to the
public domain by waiving all of their rights to the work worldwide under
copyright law, including all related and neighbouring rights, to the extent
allowed by law.

You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial
purposes, all without asking permission.

Covered here:

    repertory/bryant-pocket-1900.json
    repertory/clarke-clinical-1900.json
    repertory/drake-foot-sweat-1894.json
    repertory/hering-repertory-1889.json
    repertory/humphreys-sexual-1860.json
    repertory/jahr-repertory-1847.json
    repertory/kent-1897/
    repertory/lippe-repertory-1879.json
    repertory/pulford-rheumatism-1898.json
    repertory/sensation-as-if-1890.json
    repertory/vilas-eye-ear-1890.json
    materia_medica/

These are compilations of source texts published before 1929 and therefore in
the public domain.  Please credit the authors of the source texts and the
compiler, Dr Sohil Momin.  See CREDITS.md.

Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

--------------------------------------------------------------------
2.  repertory/repertorium-publicum-2008/  —  GNU GPL v3   (NOT CC0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
This folder is third-party material and is NOT covered by the CC0 dedication
above:

    Repertorium Publicum (2008), Vladimir Polony — an open, Kent-derived
    repertory published as part of the OpenRep source code under the GNU
    General Public License v3.

It is not public domain, and it is not this compiler's work to relicense.  It
remains under GPL v3.  Any use or redistribution of these files must comply with
GPL v3, including its copyleft requirement that derivative works are licensed
under GPL v3.

    Full text: LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt  (or https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt)
    Source   : https://github.com/nondeterministic/oorep

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Redistributing the whole repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------
If you redistribute the repository as a whole, both licences apply and GPL v3 is
the stricter of the two: GPL v3 governs any use of
repertory/repertorium-publicum-2008/, while everything else remains CC0.

GPL v3 permits commercial use.  It requires that derivative works stay under
GPL v3 and that the corresponding source is made available.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Warranty
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Both licences disclaim warranties.  The data is provided "as is", and the
accuracy of the underlying OCR and transcriptions is not guaranteed.
